The 1924–25 Scottish football season was [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]]'s 37th season of competitive football, in which they competed in the [[Scottish First Division]]<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.londonhearts.com/scores/a1920/celtic1925.htm|title=Results for Celtic for 1924-25|website=www.londonhearts.com}}</ref> and the [[Scottish Cup]].

In the league, they dropped to 4th place from 3rd the previous season, below [[Hibernian F.C.|Hibernian]], [[Airdrieonians F.C. (1878)|Airdrieonians]] and three-in-a-row champions [[Rangers F.C.|Rangers]].

However, their Scottish Cup campaign was way more fruitful as they successfully reclaimed the trophy. They were crowned cup champions for the 11th time in the club's history, their 27th major domestic honour.

Celtic won [[1925 Scottish Cup final|the final]] 2-1 against [[Dundee F.C.|Dundee]], with goals by [[Patrick Gallacher]] and [[Jimmy McGrory]]. Previously, they had defeated [[Rangers F.C.|Rangers]] 5-0 in the semi-final, [[St Mirren F.C.|St. Mirren]] in a 4th round second replay, and [[Solway Star F.C.|Solway Star]], [[Alloa Athletic F.C.|Alloa Athletic]] and [[Third Lanark A.C.|Third Lanark]] in the early rounds.

